  "habitat": "Pairs and small parties in dry thornveld, dry watercourses, bare ground under bushes and kraals. Never far from water.",
  "summary": "A very common resident. Brown above, with powder-blue underparts of variable extent. The immature is paler than the female and has a black bill. It calls a high-pitched weet-weet on the ground and in flight, and also has a complicated song. It is nomadic and moves into suburbia in dry winters. The Kemp code RB was left unchanged.",
